@*
    A view that exists in the catalog but has no handler yet (tasks 3.3 and 3.4 fill these in).

    It renders inside the shell rather than as a bare 501 body so the navigation stays usable --
    a reader who lands here must be able to leave without pressing Back. The response still carries
    501, because the page is an explanation and not the view that was asked for.

    This file is temporary by design. When every view is wired, the switch in DumpRoutes has no
    default case left to reach and this fragment can be deleted along with NotWiredYet.
*@
@model ViewDescriptor

<div id="v-@Model.Name">
    <div class="dn-empty">
        <div class="dn-empty__title">@Model.Title is not built yet.</div>
        <div class="dn-view-desc">
            SOS <code class="dn-code">@Model.Command</code> — @Model.Description
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
